# PageProjection — absolute accept

**Bar:** Projected Live (`MirrorMode.PageProjection`) must be **1:1** with opening the same site in a normal browser on Virtual. **DOM** = numerical/state 1:1. **CSSOM live** = perceived 1:1 (eventual; not 60 Hz lockstep of every rule mutation). Establish/resync CSSOM still complete. Full text: `docs/page-projection/spec/acceptance.md`. Index: `docs/page-projection/spec/README.md`. Protocol: `docs/page-projection/spec/frame-protocol.md`. Observability/probes: `docs/page-projection/spec/observability.md`. Open bugs: `docs/page-projection/spec/open.md`. **Do not implement from `docs/page-projection/archive/`.**

## Hard bans

- **No ad-hoc workarounds — carved in stone / strictly forbidden** on the establish/sync path (no “bootstrap DomMap dump” to paper over a broken stream). Fix seed / table apply / resync ([acceptance.md](docs/page-projection/spec/acceptance.md) T3 V4 restatement).
- Never declare PASS / “fixed” / “recovered” from protocol-only signals (`200`, `ResyncServed`, WD>N, `ownedRules`, `htmlLen`) while the surface is incomplete, slow, crushed, desynced, or unusable.
- Never pass/fail table or DOM isomorphism from event telemetry; use a coherent snapshot probe at sequence S (`observability.md`).
- Never treat a green smoke scoped to one recovery bug as site accept.
- Journal / observation / screenshots that show unusability **must fail** harness diagnose — do not ignore backlog, `armed=false`, broken imgs, unanswered Resync, or visual defects.

## Duty

When working Sessions / PageProjection / smoke / telemetry: optimize and assert for **parity**, not for green protocol hops. If parity is broken, say so plainly and keep the defect open.
